{{also|talón}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-talon.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ælən|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|/ˈtælən/|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|talon||heel, spur|lang=fro}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sharp]], [[hooked]] [[claw]] of a [[bird of prey]] or other [[predatory]] [[animal]].
#: {{rfquotek|Francis Bacon}}
# {{context|zoology|lang=en}} One of certain small prominences on the hind part of the face of an elephant's tooth.
# {{context|architecture|lang=en}} A kind of moulding, concave at the bottom and convex at the top; an [[ogee]]. (When the concave part is at the top, it is called an ''inverted talon''.)
# The shoulder of the bolt of a lock on which the key acts to shoot the bolt.
#: {{rfquotek|Knight}}
# In the card game [[bezique]], the remaining stock of [[undealt]] cards.

